"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KRHHE8G71S0VYD8\",\"title\":\"Tupande — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Tupande\",\"Terraton\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2027\",\"Project code\",\"BXDD\",\"Crediting period\",\"15 Aug 2026 to 15 Aug 2036\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"BXDD\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2027\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"24 Jul 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"14 Jul 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://terraton.ai\",\"t\":\"Terraton\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-requirements\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KOmLuhU6yzCYYtUWPyQCw4aByEEJ7Q1-/view\",\"t\":\"VVB Policy\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2/prj_1KRHHE8G71S0VYD8/pjd_1KY9MM3Y21S0C33M/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2/prj_1KRHHE8G71S0VYD8/pjd_1KXFMD5Q91S0SP6E/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nTupande\\nTerraton\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2027\\nProject code\\nBXDD\\nCrediting period\\n15 Aug 2026 to 15 Aug 2036\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nThe Tupande biochar project in Kirinyaga County, Kenya converts macadamia nut shell waste into biochar. The facility expects to produce 2,352 tonnes of biochar annually. This biochar will be distributed to smallholder farmers within the approved project boundary as a soil amendment to improve crop yields and soil health while sequestering carbon for 200+ years.\\n\\nKirinyaga County\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 23 Jul 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nAudit kick-off\\n\\nA Validation & Verification Body (VVB) officially commences the project validation and verification process. All VVBs are approved and appointed by Isometric based on the requirements outlined in the Isometric Standard and VVB Policy.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2027\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2027\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n24 Jul 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Jul 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"